    "answer": {
      "short": "$70$ triangles.\n\nChoose two points on one line and one on the other; add the two cases.",
      "worked": "A triangle must have two vertices on one line and one on the other. Three points on the same line do not form a triangle.\n\nTwo vertices on $A$ and one on $B$: $\\binom{4}{2}\\binom{5}{1}=30$.\n\nOne vertex on $A$ and two on $B$: $\\binom{4}{1}\\binom{5}{2}=40$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{4}{2}\\binom{5}{1}+\\binom{4}{1}\\binom{5}{2}\\\\N&=30+40\\\\N&=70\\end{align*}$$\nThere are $70$ triangles.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
